    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0286" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Baron
                            Saurma.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of yesterday in relation to the provisions of Schedule E,
                    182½, of the new tariff act, touching the levying in certain cases of an
                    additional duty of one-tenth of a cent per pound on sugar from countries that
                    pay a bounty thereon.</p>
                <p>As soon as I have opportunity to give due consideration to the important question
                    and take the President’s direction thereon, I will do myself the honor to reply
                    to your note.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
